                <pb facs="0332" n="308" xml:id="pg308"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Funchal,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Excellent Sir:</hi> In compliance with the
                    orders received from your excellency, I have intimated the commander of the war
                    steamer Florida to leave this port within twenty-four hours, and in reply to
                    said intimation I have received from said officer a communication, of which I
                    have the honor of transmitting a copy to your excellency, wherein the said
                    commander declares he was forced to come into this port in want of water, bread,
                    and coals, and that, consequently, it is impossible for him to quit this port
                    without those articles.</p>
                <p>Your excellency will decide whatever is just, and I await your excellency’s
                    orders on this head.</p>
                <p>God preserve your excellency.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOAQUIN PEDRO DE CASTELBRANCO, <hi rendition="#italic">Post Captain R.
                            N. and Captain of the Port.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Dn. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacintho Antonio
                        Perdigao</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Civil Governor of the Funchal
                            District.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
